ublic","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-28T16:57:18Z","updated_at":"2023-08-28T16:57:18Z","body":"@mistotebe and I are python-ldap maintainers.\r\nPersonally, I'm okay with `python-ldap` name for the license. @mistotebe ?\r\n\r\nAlso, should we use https://github.com/python-ldap/python-ldap URL for the license instead?\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1696031393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1697195668","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2056#issuecomment-1697195668","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2056","id":1697195668,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85lKSaU","user":{"login":"mistotebe","id":1913139,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTMxMzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1913139?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistotebe","html_url":"https://github.com/mistotebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistotebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistotebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistotebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistotebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistotebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistotebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistotebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistotebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistotebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-29T10:43:41Z","updated_at":"2023-08-29T10:43:41Z","body":"`python-ldap` sounds appropriate if that's where the license originated, sure.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1697195668/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1710780694","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2056#issuecomment-1710780694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2056","id":1710780694,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85l-HEW","user":{"login":"Pizza-Ria","id":46799628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Nzk5NjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46799628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria","html_url":"https://github.com/Pizza-Ria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-07T21:16:13Z","updated_at":"2023-09-07T21:16:13Z","body":"I honestly don't know what to do with this language \"The python-ldap package is distributed under Python-style license.\"  I agree it is fairly permissive but it also says that it was tested with Python 2.0 so I'm assuming that means the Python 2.0 License would have applied to that test???  That includes the BeOpen and CNRI - is that what is intended by a Python-style license?  I'm not sure that this is a specific license itself but more permission to use a python-ish license???  Currently disinclined to add. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1710780694/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1710801170","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2056#issuecomment-1710801170","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2056","id":1710801170,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85l-MES","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-07T21:38:30Z","updated_at":"2023-09-07T21:38:30Z","body":"@Pizza-Ria the basic issue here is, what does \"Python-style license\" mean in this case. One possible interpretation is how I'd usually approach a case of a (non-PSF) Python library being licensed as \"Python\", which is to suppose that the top license in the Python-2.0.1 stack applies (the PSF-2.0 license) but with all the references to \"Python Software Foundation\" implicitly substituted. In the case of python-ldap, however, we have what I think is a long period of the maintainers applying a looser interpretation. The maintainers note that it is basically not possible to change the license of this project and they are clearly doing their best to give it a reasonable and flexible reading. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1710801170/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1710995522","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2056#issuecomment-1710995522","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2056","id":1710995522,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85l-7hC","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","recei